{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966798,"nonce":"X4FNQsgqpbngglbx64QOncmoPeI=","title":"OverlayBuilder::at(x, y)` places verbatim — no auto-flip or viewport clamp. Popovers","message":"`OverlayBuilder::popover().at(x, y).show()` places the overlay's\ntop-left at exactly `(x, y)`. `OverlayPosition::AtPoint` in\n`overlay_stack.rs` does NOT clamp against the window viewport or\nflip to the opposite side when the popover would overflow. Callers\nanchoring \"below the trigger\" must compute the placement themselves\nagainst the viewport size.\n\n**Symptom:** A popover anchored under a trigger near the bottom of\nthe window scrolls off-screen; the Done button / hex input / any\naction below the wheel becomes unreachable. The user can see the\nwheel but can't confirm or dismiss without hitting Escape.\n\n**Where to get viewport dimensions:**\n`blinc_core::context_state::BlincContextState::get().viewport_size()`\nreturns `(w, h)` in logical pixels. Set by `windowed.rs` on\nresize / first paint.\n\n**Recipe (used in node_editor_demo's color picker popover):**\n1. Estimate popover bounding box (wheel/content + chrome\n   padding + gaps). Err on the high side so the flip kicks in\n   before the user sees a clipped frame.\n2. If `place_y + EST_POPOVER_H \u003e viewport.h`, flip to\n   `anchor.y() - EST_POPOVER_H - 4` and set\n   `AnchorDirection::Top`.\n3. If `place_x + EST_POPOVER_W \u003e viewport.w`, shift left so the\n   right edge sits at `viewport.w - margin`.\n4. Floor both axes at a small margin (8 px) so the popover never\n   touches the chrome.\n\n**Resolved 2026-06-19** by baking the clamp into\n`position_wrapper`'s `OverlayPosition::AtPoint` branch in\n`crates/blinc_layout/src/widgets/overlay_stack.rs`. When the caller\nsets `.size(w, h)` on the OverlayBuilder, the resolver clamps x\nagainst the right edge and flips y above the trigger when the\nbottom would overflow. Without a size hint the legacy\n`outer.left(x).top(y)` placement still applies — callers opt in by\nsupplying a bounding-box estimate.\n\n`cn::context_menu` adopted the hint (items.len() * (font + padding)\ngives `est_height`, `min_width` is `est_width`). Adoption needed\nfor: `cn::popover`, `cn::dropdown_menu`, `cn::menubar`,\n`cn::hover_card`, `cn::navigation_menu`. Recipe is one-liner:\n`.size(EST_W, EST_H)` between `.at(...)` and `.show()` with\ngenerous-side estimates.\n\nSee also feedback 4px unit grid — sibling concern (spacing\ninside the same popover); gotcha overlay canvas z interleave\nfor layering inside an overlay.","files":null}]}